"Add Rumi to your channel as admin and it keeps an eye on it for you. It never spams your channel.\n\n<b>How to start</b>\n1. Tap Add to your channel on /start.\n2. Pick your channel and keep the suggested admin rights.\n3. Rumi posts one short Protected by Rumi message with two buttons.\n\n<b>What the channel sees</b>\nOne post when Rumi joins, then one short post every 2 days. Each deletes itself after 3.5 hours, so your feed stays clean. Nothing else is ever posted there.\n\n<b>What you get privately</b>\nEvery few hours Rumi checks your member count. If it drops a lot (10 members or 10 percent, whichever is bigger), Rumi sends you one private message with the old and new count. Every week you also get a short summary with your member count and the change. You must have pressed /start with Rumi once so it can message you.\n\n<b>Example</b>\nYour channel goes from 500 to 430 members overnight. You get a private message: went from 500 to 430, minus 70.\n\n<b>What Rumi cannot do</b>\nTelegram gives bots no control over reports, so Rumi does not claim to block them. It helps you notice trouble early.\n\n<b>Good to know</b>\nRemoving Rumi from the channel stops all checks. Your data for that channel is deleted.": ""
